  "question": {
    "text": "The lengths of the sides of a triangle are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. If for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, the area of the triangle is maximum, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
